# template-services — project context

NestJS API paired with **template-platform** (sibling repo). Replace env vars and copy when forking.

## Stack

- NestJS 10, Mongoose, Passport JWT + Google OAuth, class-validator
- Global prefix: `/api/v1`
- MongoDB via `MONGODB_URI`

## Modules (template scope)

- **`auth`**: register, login, refresh, logout, Google OAuth, password reset, `GET /auth/me`, user API tokens
- **`users`**: `GET /users/me`, admin list/get/patch
- **`sessions`**: refresh-token session store
- **`emails`**: Resend transactional mail
- **`user-api-tokens`**: PAT create/list/revoke; `JwtOrUserPatGuard` for JWT or PAT auth
- **`common`**: `RolesGuard`, shared decorators/pipes

## Auth guards

| Pattern | Guard / decorator |
|---------|-------------------|
| Required session | `JwtAuthGuard` |
| Public + optional session | `OptionalJwtAuthGuard`, `@OptionalUser()` |
| JWT or PAT (automation) | `JwtOrUserPatGuard` (from `UserApiTokensModule`) |
| Role check (after auth) | `RolesGuard`, `@Roles()` |

See **`docs/GUARDS.md`** and **`docs/role-guard-implementation.md`**. New feature modules: **`docs/MODULES.md`**. Frontend public routes: **template-platform** `AuthGuard` + `src/proxy.ts`.

## Conventions

- User roles: `user` | `admin` (`UserRole` in `users/schemas/user.schema.ts`)
- Username: lowercase `a-z`, digits, underscore; validated in `UsernameService`
- JWT payload: `sub`, `email`, `role`, `accountTier`
- Google callback redirects to `{FRONTEND_URL}/auth/google/callback` with `token`, `refresh`, `role`, optional `state`

## Platform client

The web app calls this API at `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (typically `http://localhost:3001/api/v1` in dev). Read **template-platform** for UI routes and `ServicesProvider`.
